RT64 4337374 (after rt64-present-capture-widescreen.patch): two-player split screens in widescreen (v0.2).

RT64 widens a 3D view (stretched viewport, aspect-adjusted projection) only when its viewport spans the whole width of the
framebuffer pair's scissor and is wider than tall. A side-by-side split screen draws two views, each half the width and
taller than wide, so both stay in the centred 4:3 area. With RT64::splitScreenWide set (the host sets it; default off,
upstream behaviour), a view that fills one side of the pair's scissor up to its middle and most of its height, in a pair
that has such a view on both sides, is widened like a full-width view, in FramebufferRenderer and ProjectionProcessor
alike, and a fill rect covering such a half (a per-view clear) is stretched with it. A lone half-width view (a model on a
menu screen) keeps the upstream rule. With RT64::splitScreenBlackBands set (the host sets it; default off) and
splitScreenWide off (the host's `split = original`), a pair with views on both halves keeps its side bands black: a whole-width colour fill clears the stretched rect to black, then its own colour
over the 4:3 area only (the game's frame clear, often the sky colour, filled the bands around the two 4:3 views). New header
src/render/rt64_split_screen.h (the rules and three counters); the fill call gets innerRect / bandsBlack.
Patched lines are marked [thps-recomp].
